Nevertheless, your original statement ("A lawful valkyrie, usually, is a
dwarven walkyrie.") was correct as it stood, based on a misunderstanding
or not. At least, it is correct unless we assume that the people who
manually choose their characters prefer human Valks over dwarven Valks
by rather large numbers. (I suspect the reverse may be somewhat true.)
In randomly generated characters, though, lawful dwarven Valks outnumber
lawful human Valks two to one.
The reason for this is simple: the RNG chooses character traits in the
same order that you do manually, and at each state it picks its option
from the still available combinations, with percentages based _only_ on
the options it has at that stage, not on any later ones. Nor are the
percentages altered by previous stages. Illegal combinations are ruled
out completely; the percentages for legal combinations are divided
equally _at that stage alone_.

So it starts by picking role. This results in a whole host of non-Valks,
whom we will ignore, and some Valks. Then it chooses race. It can now
choose human or dwarven, and will pick either with 50% chance - nor will
anything retroactively adjust those odds later on. So we now have 50%
human Valks and 50% dwarven Valks.
Next up is alignment, and here the numbers get skewed. You see, for
those 50% human Valks it has to choose between lawful and neutral, and
it chooses, again, without regards for the percentages at the race
stage, an equitable 50% either way. We now have 25% lawful human Valks
and 25% neutral human Valks. For dwarves, though, there is nothing to
choose - _all_ dwarves are lawful, so we have 50% lawful dwarven Valks
out of the total.
The final step is unique for Valks, because unlike any other role they
can only be female, but this has no bearing on the question at hand. We
still end up with our Valks divided in 50% lawful dwarven, 25% lawful
human, and 25% neutral human. Which is, you'll have noticed, twice as
many lawful dwarven Valks as lawful human Valks.

And that means that yes, even in the latest version, if you run a
randomly rolled lawful Valkyrie, the odds are exactly two to one that
she'll be a dwarf.

